  "verdict": "On one SHE scale at B3LYP/C-PCM the device chloro couple against the flavin couple at 32's protocol gives a downhill cascade of +255 mV against +529 mV measured for the same free couples; of the 274 mV between them +209 mV lie on the acceptor side and +65 mV on the donor side. Relaxing the flavin, then adding its ZPE, then its RRHO free energy moves the donor side to +101 · -210 · -199 mV, and the device cascade to +218 · +529 · +519 mV — the screening donor side (+65 mV) does not survive the zero-point term it omits. Within 50 mV of the measured cascade while each side is ≥ 100 mV off — an agreement by CANCELLATION, not a validation: «chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed + ZPE (-0.3 mV = donor -210 + acceptor +209); «chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed + RRHO free energy (+10.2 mV = donor -199 + acceptor +209); «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed + ZPE (-26.8 mV = donor -210 + acceptor +183); «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed + RRHO free energy (-16.3 mV = donor -199 + acceptor +183). Every form is downhill at every donor level; the acceptor side is smallest for «chloro + 3 H₂O on Cl⁻» (+7 mV), and «aqua (methodological reference)», «bis-imidazole (brush-presented, hypothetical)» overshoot the measured mediator. The ZPE and RRHO levels correct the donor of every form and the Os side of «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» only (96): with both sides relaxed and corrected that form gives +245 · +596 · RRHO not comparable mV (electronic · ZPE · RRHO); every other form's ZPE/RRHO cascade is one-sided. The device cascade (+574 mV) adds the measured protein shift (-45 mV on the donor), which is not computed here. Every cell shares B3LYP, C-PCM, |SHE_abs| = 4.281 V and a scalar-relativistic Os, which the cells cannot test: spin–orbit coupling on Os, the one omitted term of known sign, reverses a cell beyond 218 mV; at the size ref 63 computes for [Os(bipy)₃] itself (-250 mV, its SI, the closest ligand set it treats) it turns 2 of the 32 cells uphill («chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -32 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -5 mV), at the abstract's octahedral summary (-300 mV) 5, and at the larger rows of its Table S2 up to 10 (−400 mV) («chloro (device, programmatic)» at MMFF geometries, electronic (32) → -45 mV; «chloro (device, programmatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -82 mV; «chloro + 1 H₂O on Cl⁻» at relaxed, electronic → -18 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at MMFF geometries, electronic (32) → -18 mV; «chloro, both states relaxed (adiabatic)» at relaxed, electronic → -55 mV); the alternative 4.44 V convention (-159 mV) alone 0, with spin–orbit coupling 10 ⊥ 12 (the [Os(bipy)₃] ⊥ octahedral value); against the measured free flavin the spin–orbit-shifted device couple lies at +70 ⊥ +20 mV and turns uphill past -320 mV — so with spin–orbit coupling at any of those sizes the protocol does not determine the sign of the device cascade. At ωB97X/def2-TZVP on both sides (the device form only — B1 with 112's flavin) the device cascade is -137 · +174 · +164 mV (relaxed electronic · + ZPE · + RRHO, the last two one-sided): the device cell's direction on the relaxed electronic flavin level does not survive the higher tier."
